1
00:00:59,320 --> 00:00:59,920
Um...

2
00:01:00,719 --> 00:01:02,719
How did Second Madam die?

3
00:01:04,719 --> 00:01:05,680
Second Madam...

4
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:07,359
She broke the Demon-Revealing Mirror

5
00:01:07,640 --> 00:01:08,680
and was haunted by an evil spirit.

6
00:01:09,640 --> 00:01:11,079
Go see if Master is back yet.

7
00:01:11,560 --> 00:01:12,239
Yes, Madam.

8
00:01:19,959 --> 00:01:21,319
The Flower Demon killed someone!

9
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:33,439
Demon-Revealing Mirror, keep us safe.

10
00:01:33,959 --> 00:01:35,280
Monsters and ghosts, be gone!

11
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Alright, alright, alright.

12
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:39,359
Why wave a mirror around at this hour?

13
00:01:39,519 --> 00:01:40,200
Let me tell you,

14
00:01:40,359 --> 00:01:41,799
careful not to summon all three wives.

15
00:01:42,879 --> 00:01:43,599
So,

16
00:01:43,879 --> 00:01:44,640
Second Madam

17
00:01:45,159 --> 00:01:47,000
was really crushed by the chandelier?

18
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:48,640
I saw it with my own eyes.

19
00:01:49,359 --> 00:01:51,599
The chandelier came crashing right down.

20
00:01:52,599 --> 00:01:54,439
Second Madam was such a beautiful woman,

21
00:01:55,560 --> 00:01:57,640
yet she was crushed to pieces.

22
00:01:58,760 --> 00:01:59,640
It was so tragic.

23
00:02:00,760 --> 00:02:03,120
Don't wander around the manor at night.

24
00:02:03,599 --> 00:02:04,760
If you run into Second Madam,

25
00:02:04,920 --> 00:02:05,599
you'll be in trouble.

26
00:02:07,439 --> 00:02:08,319
One night,

27
00:02:08,960 --> 00:02:10,639
Xiaocui ran into Second Madam.

28
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:14,240
She was scared sick and is now bedridden.

29
00:02:20,360 --> 00:02:21,520
Where did Second Madam live?

30
00:02:22,520 --> 00:02:23,439
The West Wing.

31
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:25,400
The West Wing.

32
00:02:25,840 --> 00:02:26,240
Alright.

33
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:27,479
Let's go take a look.

34
00:03:06,759 --> 00:03:07,280
Second Madam,

35
00:03:08,599 --> 00:03:10,360
did you return from studying in France

36
00:03:11,199 --> 00:03:12,319
and immediately marry into the Li family?

37
00:03:19,919 --> 00:03:20,680
Do you

38
00:03:21,520 --> 00:03:23,159
put on makeup every day before going out?

39
00:03:30,120 --> 00:03:31,000
But why

40
00:03:32,199 --> 00:03:32,960
would this chandelier

41
00:03:33,439 --> 00:03:34,680
happen to fall right on you?

42
00:03:56,039 --> 00:03:57,280
This vanity has been moved.

43
00:03:59,240 --> 00:04:00,240
It should've been further inside,

44
00:04:01,719 --> 00:04:02,919
but someone dragged it here.

45
00:04:04,680 --> 00:04:06,000
Furniture moving late at night...

46
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:09,560
Someone must've tied a rope to drag it.

47
00:04:11,199 --> 00:04:12,879
The furniture was dragged a bit each day.

48
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:14,039
Over time,

49
00:04:15,199 --> 00:04:17,519
it ended up right under the chandelier.

50
00:04:18,279 --> 00:04:19,360
Second Madam wasn't one for details,

51
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:21,560
so she wouldn't have noticed.

52
00:04:23,120 --> 00:04:23,879
But this chandelier...

53
00:04:23,959 --> 00:04:25,399
how did it fall out of nowhere

54
00:04:25,720 --> 00:04:27,000
and happen to hit Second Madam?

55
00:04:27,639 --> 00:04:28,160
Look here.

56
00:04:29,399 --> 00:04:30,240
A scorched hemp rope.

57
00:04:31,959 --> 00:04:33,399
If my deduction is correct,

58
00:04:34,360 --> 00:04:35,639
the weapon used to kill Second Madam

59
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:37,839
must still be in this room.

60
00:04:38,519 --> 00:04:39,480
What could the weapon be?

61
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:43,639
The murder took place

62
00:04:44,399 --> 00:04:45,480
at 1:00 PM.

63
00:04:46,279 --> 00:04:46,920
The angle of the sunlight

64
00:04:47,040 --> 00:04:48,240
should be around 80 degrees.

65
00:04:49,879 --> 00:04:51,319
If my deduction is correct,

66
00:04:52,560 --> 00:04:54,040
the weapon used to kill Second Madam

67
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:55,920
is this magnifying glass.

68
00:04:58,639 --> 00:05:00,839
An old book in Wenchang Pavilion says

69
00:05:01,639 --> 00:05:02,240
that a magnifying glass

70
00:05:03,199 --> 00:05:04,319
can focus light.

71
00:05:05,240 --> 00:05:05,800
And the killer

72
00:05:05,959 --> 00:05:07,040
used this principle

73
00:05:08,160 --> 00:05:09,560
to focus sunlight into a single point.

74
00:05:10,279 --> 00:05:11,279
Then, using the vanity mirror,

75
00:05:11,759 --> 00:05:12,839
they reflected it onto the hemp rope,

76
00:05:13,680 --> 00:05:15,000
causing the rope to burn

77
00:05:15,639 --> 00:05:16,399
and the chandelier to fall.

78
00:05:17,240 --> 00:05:17,920
I know about this!

79
00:05:18,319 --> 00:05:19,560
If you point a magnifying glass at wood,

80
00:05:19,720 --> 00:05:20,439
it'll catch fire in a bit.

81
00:05:20,920 --> 00:05:23,040
So the killer used the room's furnishings

82
00:05:23,199 --> 00:05:24,079
as a murder weapon.

83
00:05:25,199 --> 00:05:26,920
They could kill without being present.

84
00:05:28,839 --> 00:05:29,800
And before this,

85
00:05:30,680 --> 00:05:31,800
they ran multiple experiments,

86
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:33,639
which is why the vase heated up

87
00:05:33,720 --> 00:05:35,040
and shattered.

88
00:05:38,160 --> 00:05:40,120
How did the stool Master sat on break?

89
00:05:40,439 --> 00:05:42,600
To execute this plan precisely,

90
00:05:43,519 --> 00:05:45,519
the killer even tampered with the rope.

91
00:05:47,079 --> 00:05:48,240
To cut the hemp rope,

92
00:05:49,160 --> 00:05:50,240
they stepped on and broke the stool.

93
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:53,160
Why would the killer go to such lengths

94
00:05:53,439 --> 00:05:54,600
to kill Second Madam?

95
00:06:06,639 --> 00:06:07,040
Dazhu.

96
00:06:08,120 --> 00:06:08,639
Let me ask you something.

97
00:06:09,639 --> 00:06:11,920
At 1:00 PM on the day Second Madam died,

98
00:06:12,399 --> 00:06:15,000
did she arrange to meet Master at home?

99
00:06:16,120 --> 00:06:17,920
Second Madam made some suits for Master.

100
00:06:19,639 --> 00:06:21,199
She called him home to try them on.

101
00:06:22,279 --> 00:06:23,319
Master had no choice but to agree.

102
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:24,959
Take care.

103
00:06:25,439 --> 00:06:25,839
Okay.

104
00:06:27,079 --> 00:06:29,199
But as Master was about to close shop,

105
00:06:29,720 --> 00:06:30,680
someone came into the store.

106
00:06:32,959 --> 00:06:34,600
I'm meeting my wife. I have to go.

107
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:35,600
Sir,

108
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:36,839
please come back later.

109
00:06:37,639 --> 00:06:39,079
I have a big deal

110
00:06:39,399 --> 00:06:40,759
that I can only discuss with you.

111
00:06:43,959 --> 00:06:44,959
What big deal?

112
00:06:59,720 --> 00:07:00,240
Master.

113
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:01,480
Master, terrible news!

114
00:07:01,800 --> 00:07:02,920
Second Madam is dead.

115
00:07:03,639 --> 00:07:04,279
What?

116
00:07:06,720 --> 00:07:08,000
By a twist of fate,

117
00:07:09,079 --> 00:07:10,759
Master Li escaped disaster yet again.

118
00:07:12,360 --> 00:07:13,120
Mengzhu,

119
00:07:13,240 --> 00:07:14,439
First Wife, Second Madam...

120
00:07:15,079 --> 00:07:16,560
All three of them were scapegoats.

121
00:07:16,959 --> 00:07:18,160
There's an evil spirit in this mansion.

122
00:07:19,439 --> 00:07:20,759
Master is generous and charitable.

123
00:07:21,120 --> 00:07:22,360
He is protected by the gods.

124
00:07:23,319 --> 00:07:25,519
Good deeds are always rewarded.

125
00:07:26,360 --> 00:07:27,079
Alright, alright.

126
00:07:27,560 --> 00:07:28,680
Dazhu, go back to sleep.

127
00:07:36,199 --> 00:07:36,959
Master.

128
00:07:37,279 --> 00:07:39,839
Did you see a child in your vision?

129
00:07:41,040 --> 00:07:41,759
He was right there.

130
00:07:49,040 --> 00:07:50,199
On this wall...

131
00:07:51,519 --> 00:07:52,839
it wasn't this painting before.

132
00:07:54,360 --> 00:07:55,319
It was a wooden puppet.

133
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:57,480
And now this painting is here.

134
00:07:59,319 --> 00:07:59,959
It seems

135
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:02,600
someone is guiding our investigation.

136
00:08:05,279 --> 00:08:07,959
What do they want us to investigate then?
